public class LivelockDemo {
    static volatile boolean aYields = true;
    static volatile boolean bYields = true;

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Each thread keeps stepping aside for the other -> active, but no progress
        Runnable a = () -> {
            while (bYields) { Thread.onSpinWait(); } // busy-waiting, not blocked
            System.out.println("A proceeds");
        };
        Runnable b = () -> {
            while (aYields) { Thread.onSpinWait(); }
            System.out.println("B proceeds");
        };
        new Thread(a).start();
        new Thread(b).start();
    }
}
```

In deadlock both threads sit idle in BLOCKED. In livelock both run flat out yet neither finishes — fix it by breaking symmetry (randomized backoff or lock ordering).

